# A rule carries its own proof: check runs every Example against its rule
# alone, and a failing one exits 1 without being a validation error.

# An untrusted shared tier's Examples run like any other tier's, and a failure
# there exits 1, while its rules stay out of the effective ruleset.
exec sh -c 'handrail check; echo code=$?'
stdout '^code=1$'
stderr 'run handrail trust'
stderr 'drifted\.md: line 11: match example fails: command="sudo rm -rf /"'
! stdout drifted
exec sh -c 'handrail check --json; echo code=$?'
stdout '^code=1$'
stdout '"path": ".*/drifted\.md",\n +"message": "line 11: match example fails: command=\\"sudo rm -rf /\\""'

exec handrail trust
exec sh -c 'handrail check; echo code=$?'
stdout '^code=1$'
stdout '^project-shared +drifted +PreToolUse +shell +block +enabled$'
stderr 'drifted\.md: line 11: match example fails: command="sudo rm -rf /"'
! stderr 'passing\.md'
stderr 'list-fails\.md: line 8: no_match example fails: url=\["https://docs.example/" "https://evil.example/"\]'

# A url list is one Candidate per entry, and each derives its domain.
! stderr 'domains\.md'

# A path list is a rename, source and destination, and a written path is
# cleaned as a live one is.
! stderr 'renames\.md'

# An Example has no harness, so a tool name carries every Spelling an Adapter
# gives it: Claude Code's Agent answers to Task.
! stderr 'former-names\.md'

# A shell Example yields the file payloads a live shell call yields, the edits
# of a patch heredoc Codex intercepts included; without kind: shell it takes
# the rule's kind and yields none.
! stderr 'env-files\.md'

# An Example derives unreadable as a live call does, merged with a written
# one, and every value is text: equals: true needs no quotes.
! stderr 'fail-closed\.md'
! stderr 'writes-empty\.md'

# A quoted list entry is one value however many colons it holds, and a tab
# after a key's colon still opens a mapping.
! stderr 'quoted-rename\.md'

# --json carries each rule's passed count and every failing Example's fields.
exec sh -c 'handrail check --json; echo code=$?'
stdout '^code=1$'
stdout '"examples": \{\n +"passed": 1,\n +"failed": \[\n +\{\n +"expect": "match",\n +"fields": \{\n +"command": "sudo rm -rf /"\n +\}'
stdout '"passed": 2,\n +"failed": \[\]'
stdout '"url": \[\n +"https://docs.example/",'

-- .git/HEAD --
ref: refs/heads/main
-- .handrail/drifted.md --
---
event: PreToolUse
kind: shell
action: block
conditions:
  - field: command
    starts_with: rm -rf ~
examples:
  match:
    - command: rm -rf ~
    - command: sudo rm -rf /
---
Never delete recursively from the filesystem root.
-- .handrail/passing.md --
---
event: PreToolUse
kind: shell
conditions:
  - field: command
    starts_with: rm -rf /
examples:
  match:
    - command: cd /tmp && rm -rf /
  no_match:
    - command: rm -rf ./build
---
Never delete recursively from the filesystem root.
-- .handrail/domains.md --
---
event: PreToolUse
kind: network
conditions:
  - field: domain
    equals: evil.example
examples:
  match:
    - url:
        - https://docs.example/
        - https://EVIL.example:8443/x
  no_match:
    - url: https://docs.example/
---
Not that host.
-- .handrail/renames.md --
---
event: PreToolUse
kind: file_edit
conditions:
  - field: path
    glob: "secrets/**"
examples:
  match:
    - path:
        - secrets/key
        - public/key
  no_match:
    - path: secrets/../public/key
---
Keep keys where they are.
-- .handrail/former-names.md --
---
event: PreToolUse
conditions:
  - field: tool
    equals: Task
examples:
  match:
    - tool: Agent
  no_match:
    - tool: Bash
---
Task was the old name for Agent.
-- .handrail/env-files.md --
---
event: PreToolUse
kind: file_edit
conditions:
  - field: path
    glob: "**/.env"
examples:
  match:
    - kind: shell
      command: "cd app && apply_patch <<'EOF'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: .env\n+KEY=1\n*** End Patch\nEOF"
    - kind: shell
      command: echo KEY=1 > .env
  no_match:
    - command: echo KEY=1 > .env
    - command: "apply_patch <<'EOF'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: .env\n+KEY=1\n*** End Patch\nEOF"
---
Leave .env files alone.
-- .handrail/list-fails.md --
---
event: PreToolUse
conditions:
  - field: domain
    equals: evil.example
examples:
  no_match:
    - url:
        - https://docs.example/
        - https://evil.example/
---
Not that host.
-- .handrail/fail-closed.md --
---
event: PreToolUse
action: block
conditions:
  - field: unreadable
    equals: command
examples:
  match:
    - command: bash -c "$X"
    - unreadable:
        - path
        - command
  no_match:
    - command: bash -c 'ls'
      unreadable: path
---
handrail could not read this command.
-- .handrail/writes-empty.md --
---
event: PreToolUse
kind: file_edit
conditions:
  - field: writes_empty
    equals: true
examples:
  match:
    - path: notes.txt
      writes_empty: true
  no_match:
    - path: notes.txt
      content: hello
---
This call empties a file.
-- .handrail/quoted-rename.md --
---
event: PreToolUse
kind: file_edit
conditions:
  - field:	path
    glob: "notes: *"
examples:
  match:
    - path:
        - "notes: draft.md"
        - final.md
---
A quoted entry is one value, colon and all.
